To optimize the identifier extraction function, we can enhance the regex patterns and add additional test cases to cover edge scenarios. Here's an updated version of the function:

```javascript
function extractIdentifiers(inputString) {
    const regex = /\b[a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*\b/g;
    const matches = inputString.match(regex) || [];
    return [...new Set(matches)]; // Ensure unique identifiers
}
```

Make sure to update the tests in `tests/identifierExtractor.test.js` to verify these changes:

```javascript
test('should extract unique identifiers from a string', () => {
    const input = 'var a = 0; let b = a + 1; const c = b';
    const expected = ['a', 'b', 'c'];
    expect(extractIdentifiers(input)).toEqual(expected);
});
```

Run `npm test` to verify the new tests.
